                <!-- SEC 1 -->
                <section id="sec-1" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 1.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>1. System Overview &amp; Core Architecture</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Program.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/EfDataStore.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">The <strong>MYGTS Fleet Intelligence Platform</strong> is an enterprise-grade telematics fleet management system purpose-built for GPS device lifecycle tracking, regulatory compliance across Karnataka's DMG (Mines &amp; Geology) and RTO (Regional Transport Office) departments, and full-cycle financial accounting. The platform manages over 3,900 active telematics endpoints across two strictly partitioned branches.</p>
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <strong>Architectural Foundation</strong>
                        <ul class="sec-ul" style="margin-top:8px;">
                            <li><strong>Runtime Host:</strong> ASP.NET Core MVC on .NET 10, Kestrel (port 5253), optional IIS integration.</li>
                            <li><strong>Database:</strong> SQLite 3 with <code>PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL</code> and <code>synchronous=NORMAL</code> &mdash; crash-resilient, concurrent readers, no table locking. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs</span>]</span></li>
                            <li><strong>Data Access:</strong> EF Core 9, Code-First migrations, global query filters for branch isolation. <code>IAppDataStore</code> in-memory snapshot cache for sub-millisecond reads. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/EfDataStore.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/JsonDataStore.cs</span>]</span></li>
                            <li><strong>DB Path (Runtime):</strong> <code>C:\ProgramData\MyGts_database\mygts_database.db</code> &mdash; consistent across IIS, Kestrel, and background services. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Program.cs</span>]</span></li>
                            <li><strong>Compression:</strong> Dynamic Brotli + Gzip &mdash; up to 75% payload reduction on cellular links. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Program.cs</span>]</span></li>
                            <li><strong>CSRF Protection:</strong> Anti-forgery token on all POST/PUT/DELETE. External JSON APIs use <code>[IgnoreAntiforgeryToken]</code> explicitly.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>1.1 Request Middleware Pipeline</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Program.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/SessionValidationMiddleware.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/PermissionAuthorization.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Middleware</th><th>Controlling File / Code Component</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>1</td><td>HTTPS Redirection</td><td><code>Program.cs</code> (app.UseHttpsRedirection)</td><td>Forces HTTP &rarr; HTTPS</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>2</td><td>Response Compression</td><td><code>Program.cs</code> (Brotli/Gzip provider)</td><td>Brotli/Gzip applied before static files</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>3</td><td>Static Files (wwwroot)</td><td><code>Program.cs</code> (app.UseStaticFiles)</td><td>CSS, JS, PDFs served with cache headers</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>4</td><td>Cookie Authentication</td><td><code>Program.cs</code> (AddAuthentication)</td><td>Validates HttpOnly signed session cookies</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>5</td><td>Single Active Session</td><td><code>Services/SessionValidationMiddleware.cs</code></td><td>Terminates old session when account logs in elsewhere</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>6</td><td>Authorization Middleware</td><td><code>Services/PermissionAuthorization.cs</code></td><td>ExecutiveOnly policy, RequireModulePermission filters</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>7</td><td>Global Branch Filter</td><td><code>Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs</code> (OnModelCreating)</td><td>EF Core injects WHERE Branch=&apos;{cookie}&apos; on all queries</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>8</td><td>MVC Route Dispatch</td><td><code>Program.cs</code> (MapControllerRoute)</td><td>Routes request to correct Controller/Action</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>9</td><td>15-Min Cross-Tab Idle Daemon</td><td><code>wwwroot/js/site.js</code> &bull; <code>Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml</code></td><td>Tracks real user activity, syncs across tabs via <code>localStorage.mygts_active_tick</code>, locks session after 15m true idle</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 2 -->
                <section id="sec-2" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 2.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>2. Tri-Branch Enterprise Tenant Partitioning (DMG, RTO &amp; Expenditure)</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/CoreControllers.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Areas/Expenditure/*</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">MYGTS enforces strict multi-tenancy via EF Core Global Query Filters bound to the <code>mygts_branch</code> session cookie and dedicated Area routing. Operational data is cleanly partitioned into <strong>DMG</strong> and <strong>RTO</strong>, while the <strong>Expenditure</strong> branch acts as a central financial accounting and multi-year cash flow consolidation engine.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>2.1 Branch Switch Engine &amp; Multi-Tenant Profiles</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/CoreControllers.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">SwitchBranch()</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>DMG &mdash; Mines &amp; Geology</th><th>RTO &mdash; Regional Transport</th><th>Expenditure &mdash; Financial Ledger</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><strong>Business Domain</strong></td><td>Mining haulage &amp; ore transport traceability</td><td>Public passenger &amp; AIS-140 compliance</td><td>Enterprise multi-year capital &amp; operating expenditure</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>Regulatory Body</strong></td><td>Dept. of Mines &amp; Geology, Karnataka</td><td>Regional Transport Office (MoRTH / AIS-140)</td><td>Corporate accounting &amp; fiscal audit compliance</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>Validity / Period</strong></td><td>11 months + 15 days from activation</td><td>24 months (2 years) statutory period</td><td>Fiscal Years: FY 23-24, FY 24-25, FY 25-26, FY 26-27</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>Recharge Price</strong></td><td>&#8377;2,500 standard / &#8377;3,500 reactivate</td><td>&#8377;2,000 standard / &#8377;3,000 reactivate</td><td>Tracks operational outflow vs customer cash flow</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>SIM Config</strong></td><td>Dual SIM &mdash; Airtel + BSNL fallback</td><td>Single operator (Airtel primary)</td><td>N/A (Accounting ledger)</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>Invoice Prefix</strong></td><td>INV-DMG-YYYY-NNN</td><td>INV-RTO-YYYY-NNN</td><td>EXP-YYYY-NNN &amp; Archived Proforma Invoices</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><strong>Cash Flow Integration</strong></td><td>Pushes customer receipts to ledger</td><td>Pushes customer receipts to ledger</td><td>Dynamically aggregates DMG + RTO customer receipts</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 3 -->
                <section id="sec-3" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 3.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>3. Device Registry &mdash; Hardware Field Specification</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">DeviceRecord</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Devices/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Every telematics device is stored as a <code>DeviceRecord</code> entity &mdash; the single source of truth for hardware identity, vehicle binding, SIM provisioning, certification status, and financial linkage.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>3.1 Hardware Field Schema &amp; Mutation Rules</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span>: lines 12-70 &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">Create, Edit, Details</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Controlling Code / Handling Logic</th><th>Description &amp; Business Rules</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><code>Id</code></td><td>GUID (32-hex)</td><td><span class="bg">Auto</span></td><td><code>Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N")</code></td><td>Globally unique primary key. Immutable after creation.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>SlNo</code></td><td>Numeric string</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>DevicesController.cs (MAX+1)</code></td><td>Sequential serial. Auto-incremented if omitted or '0'.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>Branch</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>ApplicationDbContext.cs</code> filter</td><td>"DMG" or "RTO". Enforces tenant boundary.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>VehicleNo</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="ba">Context</span></td><td><code>DevicesController.cs: SlashParser</code></td><td>Vehicle registration (KA35AB1234). NULL/empty = Inventory stock.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>Imei</code></td><td>15-digit string</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>SpreadsheetService.cs: ConflictCheck</code></td><td>Primary telematics hardware identity key.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>Iccid</code></td><td>19-20 digit</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>SpreadsheetService.cs</code></td><td>SIM ICCID. Dual-key conflict deduplication with IMEI.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>DeviceName</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>DevicesController.cs (Invoice prefill)</code></td><td>Model (Bharat101, FMB209). Auto-filled from linked invoice.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>Vendor</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>Controllers/VendorsController.cs</code></td><td>Vendor lookup for WhatsApp dispatch and commission attribution.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>Owner</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>Controllers/AlertsController.cs</code></td><td>Vehicle owner name. Interpolated into WhatsApp renewal messages.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>CellNo</code></td><td>10-digit</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>AlertsController.cs: PhoneCleaner</code></td><td>Owner mobile. Cleaned to digits; prefixed '91' for WhatsApp.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>SimAirtel</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>Models/DomainModels.cs</code></td><td>Airtel SIM MSISDN/ICCID for DMG dual-SIM telematics units.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>SimBsnl</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>Models/DomainModels.cs</code></td><td>BSNL SIM fallback. Used if Airtel signal unavailable.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>ActivationDate</code></td><td>ISO Date</td><td><span class="ba">Context</span></td><td><code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.CalculateExpiry()</code></td><td>First provisioned on network. Anchor for expiry calculation.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>LatestExpiryDate</code></td><td>ISO Date</td><td><span class="ba">Context</span></td><td><code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.cs</code></td><td>Subscription expiry: Activation + 11M+15D (DMG) or +24M (RTO).</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>LifecycleStatus</code></td><td>Enum string</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.SyncDevice()</code></td><td>Active, Suspension, Terminated, Dead, Inventory, Replaced.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>StockStatus</code></td><td>Enum string</td><td><span class="bg">Yes</span></td><td><code>InventoryController.cs: BulkStatus</code></td><td>New (stock), Used (deployed), Dead (faulty), Error.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>InvoiceId</code></td><td>String</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>InvoicesController.cs: LinkBatch</code></td><td>Procurement batch. 'old*' exempts device from unpaid detection.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>UnitCost</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>InvoicesController.cs -> Device.UnitCost</code></td><td>Hardware procurement cost from invoice. Used for gross margin.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>HardwareHistory</code></td><td>Text</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>DevicesController.cs: ReplaceDevicePost</code></td><td>Audit log of device swaps. Auto-appended; immutable once written.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>ExcludeFromUnpaid</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>DevicesController.cs: Filter Logic</code></td><td>Exempts legacy device from 'Unpaid Vehicles' filter.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>InformedDate</code></td><td>ISO Date</td><td><span class="bb">No</span></td><td><code>AlertsController.cs: MarkInformed</code></td><td>Date vendor notified. Suppresses duplicate alerts for the day.</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>DaysPastExpiry</code></td><td>Computed int</td><td><span class="bg">Auto</span></td><td><code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.SyncDevice()</code></td><td>Days since expiry. Drives state transitions and alert queues.</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 4 -->
                <section id="sec-4" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 4.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>4. Fleet Inventory Module</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/InventoryController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Inventory/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Inventory/BatchDetails.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Shows <strong>all hardware units registered via procurement invoices</strong>, grouped by batch &mdash; including unallocated stock, deployed units, and decommissioned hardware. A device appears in Inventory when it has a non-empty <code>InvoiceId</code>.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>4.1 Status Transitions &amp; Bulk Update Action</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/InventoryController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">BulkUpdateStatus()</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>Target Status</th><th>Database Changes</th><th>Side Effects &amp; Calculations</th><th>Handler File</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><span class="bg">Activated</span></td><td><code>StockStatus&rarr;'Used'</code>, <code>LifecycleStatus&rarr;'Active'</code></td><td>ActivationDate = today (UTC). LatestExpiryDate = <code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.CalculateExpiry()</code> using ACTIVATION_EXPIRY_MONTHS + ACTIVATION_EXPIRY_DAYS config.</td><td><code>InventoryController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="br">Dead</span></td><td><code>StockStatus&rarr;'Dead'</code>, <code>LifecycleStatus&rarr;'Dead'</code></td><td>No date changes. Device remains in Inventory for hardware audit.</td><td><code>InventoryController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="ba">Error</span></td><td><code>StockStatus&rarr;'Error'</code>, <code>LifecycleStatus&rarr;'Error'</code></td><td>Flags hardware fault. RMA/warranty return indicated.</td><td><code>InventoryController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="bb">New (Reset)</span></td><td><code>StockStatus&rarr;'New'</code>, <code>LifecycleStatus&rarr;'Inventory'</code></td><td>Clears ActivationDate and LatestExpiryDate. Returns device to unallocated stock.</td><td><code>InventoryController.cs</code></td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>4.2 Batch Grouping &amp; Color Differentiation</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/BatchColorHelper.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Inventory/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <p class="sec-p">Devices are grouped by their procurement <code>InvoiceId</code>. Each batch header displays total units, available stock (New), deployed count (Used), and faulty units (Dead/Error) with deterministic HSL batch badge colors.</p>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 5 -->
                <section id="sec-5" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 5.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>5. Device Lifecycle Engine &amp; State Machine</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">DeviceLifecycleHelper</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Implemented in <code>DeviceLifecycleHelper.SyncDevice(device, config)</code>. Called on every request that touches device data &mdash; no stale states ever appear. Conditions are evaluated IN ORDER; first match wins.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>5.1 Expiry Date Calculation Rules</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">CalculateExpiry()</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="code-block">DMG Branch:
  ExpiryDate = ActivationDate + ACTIVATION_EXPIRY_MONTHS (11) months + ACTIVATION_EXPIRY_DAYS (15) days
  Example: Activation 2026-01-15 -> Expiry 2027-01-30

RTO Branch:
  ExpiryDate = RegistrationDate + 24 Months  (statutory 2-year AIS-140 roadworthiness)</div>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>5.2 State Machine &mdash; Full Priority-Ordered Transitions</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">SyncDevice()</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>State</th><th>Trigger Condition (DPE = Days Past Expiry)</th><th>System Action &amp; Notification Trigger</th><th>Source File</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>1</td><td><span class="bb">Inventory</span></td><td>StockStatus == 'New' OR VehicleNo is blank/null</td><td>LifecycleStatus = 'Inventory'. Excluded from active fleet.</td><td><code>DevicesController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>2</td><td><span class="bg">Active</span></td><td>DPE &le; 0 (expiry is today or future)</td><td>Fully operational. Normal telematics reporting.</td><td><code>DevicesController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>3</td><td><span class="ba">Suspension</span></td><td>1 &le; DPE &le; SUSPENSION_DAYS (default: 30)</td><td>Grace period active. Services continue. Executive alert + WhatsApp template.</td><td><code>AlertsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>4</td><td><span class="br">Terminated</span></td><td>SUSPENSION_DAYS &lt; DPE &le; (SUSPENSION_DAYS + TERMINATION_DAYS) [31&ndash;50]</td><td>Carrier disconnection imminent. Reactivation fee required. Terminated alert.</td><td><code>AlertsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>5</td><td><span class="br">Dead</span></td><td>DPE &gt; SUSPENSION_DAYS + TERMINATION_DAYS (&gt;50 days)</td><td>SIM physically decommissioned. Hardware replacement indicated.</td><td><code>DevicesController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>6</td><td><span class="bp">Replaced</span></td><td>Old device when InstallType='Replacement' is processed</td><td>Permanent archive. Excluded from all live fleet views forever.</td><td><code>DevicesController.cs</code></td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>
