                <!-- SEC 8 -->
                <section id="sec-8" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 8.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>8. Hardware Replacement &amp; History Tracking</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">ReplaceDevice(), ReplaceDevicePost()</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Devices/Replace.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">When a GPS device fails or is swapped, MYGTS executes a structured replacement workflow maintaining complete audit continuity &mdash; the old record is permanently archived while a new active record is created.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>8.1 Atomic Replacement Steps &amp; Database Mutations</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">ReplaceDevicePost()</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li>Old device's <code>LifecycleStatus &rarr; "Replaced"</code> (permanently removed from all live fleet views).</li>
                        <li>Full JSON snapshot of old device stored in <code>ReplacedDeviceSnapshot</code> on new record for audit trail.</li>
                        <li><code>ReplacedDeviceId</code> = old device's GUID for relational linkage.</li>
                        <li><code>PreviousImei</code> = old device's IMEI number.</li>
                        <li><code>HardwareHistory</code> appended: <code>"Replaced from: KA35AB1234"</code>. Immutable once written.</li>
                        <li><strong>Auto-Detection:</strong> Slash format in VehicleNo (e.g., KA35AB1234/KA01AB0001) auto-extracts replacement info without manual entry. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">ParseVehicleSlash()</span>]</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 9 -->
                <section id="sec-9" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 9.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>9. Data Share &mdash; Cross-Branch Global Search</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">CrossBranchSearch()</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">IgnoreQueryFilters</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Devices/CrossBranch.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Privileged capability that bypasses the EF Core branch filter via <code>IgnoreQueryFilters()</code> to search ALL devices across ALL branches simultaneously. Used for locating IMEI ownership before a physical swap or cross-branch reconciliation.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>9.1 Search Pipeline &amp; Audit Log Structure</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">DataShareRecord</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>SharedBy / SharedByEmail / SharedByRole:</strong> Captured from logged-in session claims. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/DevicesController.cs</span>]</span></li>
                        <li><strong>SharedAt:</strong> UTC ISO 8601 timestamp of share action.</li>
                        <li><strong>VehicleNo / Imei / Iccid / DeviceBranch:</strong> Shared device identifiers.</li>
                        <li><strong>Recipient:</strong> Email/name of receiving party (entered by operator).</li>
                        <li><strong>Transaction Overlay:</strong> For each result, latest transaction per VehicleNo is fetched across branches with <code>IgnoreQueryFilters()</code>. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/TransactionsController.cs</span>]</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 10 -->
                <section id="sec-10" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 10.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>10. Transaction Ledger &amp; Payment Processing</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/TransactionsController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">TransactionRecord</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Transactions/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">The financial spine of MYGTS. Every recharge, activation, SIM renewal, and hardware payment is an immutable ledger entry with UTR tracking, vendor attribution, profit margin computation, and expiry date propagation back to the DeviceRecord.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>10.1 Key Transaction Fields &amp; Profit Engine</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/TransactionsController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">Create, Edit, CalculateProfit</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Transactions/Create.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>Amount:</strong> Total payment received from customer.</li>
                        <li><strong>Profit Formula:</strong> <code>Amount - (UnitCost + CommissionCost + SimCost)</code>. Computed automatically on transaction save.</li>
                        <li><strong>PaymentFor Types:</strong> Recharge, Reactivation, Activation, Hardware, Replacement. Aliased dynamically in search queries.</li>
                        <li><strong>Utr:</strong> Unique Bank / UPI Transaction Reference. Full-text indexed and searchable.</li>
                        <li><strong>NewExpiryDate Propagation:</strong> Automatically updates linked <code>DeviceRecord.LatestExpiryDate</code> on save. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">TransactionsController.cs</span>: lines 210-230]</span></li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>10.2 Pricing Configuration Integration</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/AdminControllers.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">Config</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/TransactionsController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>Config Key</th><th>DMG Default</th><th>RTO Default</th><th>Applied To</th><th>Source File</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><code>PRICE_RECHARGE</code></td><td>&#8377;2,500</td><td>&#8377;2,000</td><td>Standard annual GPS recharge customer price</td><td><code>ConfigRecord / TransactionsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>PRICE_REACTIVATION</code></td><td>&#8377;3,500</td><td>&#8377;3,000</td><td>Reactivation fee (device was in Terminated state)</td><td><code>ConfigRecord / TransactionsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>PRICE_TAX</code></td><td>18% (0.18)</td><td>18% (0.18)</td><td>GST tax multiplier on invoice totals</td><td><code>ConfigRecord / InvoicesController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>SIM_COST</code></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&#8377;1,300</td><td>2-year SIM subscription cost (RTO)</td><td><code>ConfigRecord / TransactionsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>COMMISSION_COST</code></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&#8377;500</td><td>Vendor commission attribution per device</td><td><code>ConfigRecord / TransactionsController.cs</code></td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>10.3 Split / Merged Payments Specification ([MERGE_PARTS: ...] Schema)</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Views/Transactions/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/TransactionsController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <p class="sec-p">When customers settle single transactions using multiple payment instruments (e.g. combined Cash + UPI or Cheque + Bank Transfer), MYGTS serializes sub-payment allocations into the record's audit metadata string:</p>
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <strong>JSON Serialization Contract (Metadata Field)</strong>
                        <pre style="margin-top:6px; font-size:0.80rem; background:#1e293b; color:#f8fafc; padding:10px; border-radius:6px; overflow-x:auto;">[MERGE_PARTS: [
  {"PartIndex": 1, "Mode": "Cash", "Amount": 3000.0, "PaidTo": "MYGTS", "Utr": "UTR-CASH-01"},
  {"PartIndex": 2, "Mode": "UPI",  "Amount": 2700.0, "PaidTo": "HDFC",  "Utr": "653863752870"}
]]</pre>
                        <ul class="sec-ul" style="margin-top:8px;">
                            <li><strong>Fallback Allocation:</strong> If historical records omit explicit part amounts, the view dynamically divides <code>Amount / parts.Count</code>.</li>
                            <li><strong>Amount Sub-Breakdown:</strong> The Amount column renders the aggregate bold total plus an inline sub-breakdown pill: <code>&#8377; 3,000 Cash + &#8377; 2,700 UPI</code>.</li>
                            <li><strong>Accordion Dropdown Sub-Row:</strong> Clicking <code>MERGED (N PAYMENTS)</code> dynamically toggles a collapsible table sub-row displaying Part #, Payment Mode, Exact Allocated Amount (&#8377;), Reference / UTR ID, and Bank Destination.</li>
                            <li><strong>Cross-Branch Availability:</strong> Fully active across both DMG and RTO branches.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 11 -->
                <section id="sec-11" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 11.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>11. Invoice &amp; Procurement Registry</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/InvoicesController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">InvoiceRecord</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Invoices/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Invoices/Details.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Hardware procurement batches. Financial anchor connecting hardware costs to device unit costs and gross margin calculations.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>11.1 Procurement Calculations &amp; Batch Auto-Provisioning</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/InvoicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">Create, AutoGenerateDevicesFromInvoice</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>CostPerDevice:</strong> Derived as <code>Amount / Quantity</code>. Propagated to <code>DeviceRecord.UnitCost</code> on invoice link. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">InvoicesController.cs</span>]</span></li>
                        <li><strong>TotalWithTaxes formula:</strong> <code>Amount + (Amount &times; PRICE_TAX) + CourierCharges</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Index KPIs:</strong> TotalValue (full spend incl. GST+freight), TotalUnits (hardware procured), TotalExtras (logistics cost), TotalBaseAmount (base hardware cost before tax). <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Views/Invoices/Index.cshtml</span>]</span></li>
                        <li><strong>Device Display Order within Invoice:</strong> StockStatus='New' first, then 'Used'/'Activated', then 'Dead', ordered by SlNoSortable.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>11.2 Multi-Dimensional Invoice Filtering Engine</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/InvoicesController.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">Index</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Invoices/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>Network Operator Query Filter:</strong> Filter invoices and proforma records matching specified SIM operators (BSNL, Airtel, Vodafone, Jio, SMT, or dynamic options).</li>
                        <li><strong>Date Range Filtering (From &amp; To Date):</strong> ISO 8601 boundary query over <code>InvoiceDate</code>, enabling custom accounting quarter and fiscal audits.</li>
                        <li><strong>Quantity Thresholds:</strong> Segment high-volume bulk hardware orders from single-device renewals.</li>
                        <li><strong>Proforma vs Tax Invoice Mode:</strong> Dynamic tab switching preserves active filters across document types.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <hr class="src-hr" />

                <!-- SEC 12 -->
                <section id="sec-12" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 12.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>12. Company Recharges &amp; Taisys Advance Tracking</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/CompanyRechargesController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/RechargesController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/CompanyRecharges/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Manages bulk advance payments made to cellular connectivity providers (e.g., Taisys). Prepaid advance batches are drawn down per-device as individual recharges are processed.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>12.1 Advance Batch Drawdown Engine &amp; Device Items</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">CompanyRechargeBatch, CompanyRechargeItem</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/CompanyRechargesController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>Total Advance Paid:</strong> Sum of <code>AdvanceAmount</code> across all batches.</li>
                        <li><strong>Total Consumed:</strong> Sum of <code>TotalAmount</code> (actual spend to date).</li>
                        <li><strong>Total Balance:</strong> Total Advance Paid &minus; Total Consumed (unspent credit remaining). <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">CompanyRechargesController.cs</span>]</span></li>
                        <li><strong>Per-unit rates:</strong> MYGTS (<code>COMPANY_RECHARGE_RATE</code> default &#8377;1,298 / <code>COMPANY_REACTIVATION_RATE</code> default &#8377;1,534) and BlueMine (<code>BLUEMINE_RECHARGE_RATE</code> default &#8377;1,156.40 / <code>BLUEMINE_REACTIVATION_RATE</code> default &#8377;1,392.40).</li>
                        <li><strong>Per-Device Item:</strong> Each batch contains one CompanyRechargeItem per device: VehicleNo, Imei, Iccid, RequestId (provider recharge ID for disputes), Amount deducted, RechargeType, Date, Status (Success/Pending/Failed).</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
