                    <div class="sec-label">Section 16.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>16. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) &amp; Security</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/AdminControllers.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/PermissionAuthorization.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/PasswordService.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Services/SessionValidationMiddleware.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Four-tier RBAC enforced at three levels: ASP.NET Core policy-based authorization, the <code>RequireModulePermission</code> action filter, and Claims-based extension methods on ClaimsPrincipal.</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>16.1 Role Definitions &amp; Permission Hierarchy</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/PermissionAuthorization.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Models/DomainModels.cs</span> (<span class="b-action">UserRecord</span>) &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Users/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <div class="tbl-wrap">
                        <table class="src-tbl">
                            <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Authority</th><th>Default Module Access</th><th>Hierarchy &amp; Visibility</th><th>Enforcement File</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><span class="br">Admin</span></td><td>System-wide root</td><td>Edit on ALL modules incl. Users, Config, Backups. Exclusive SRC access.</td><td>Can see and manage Executive, Team, User. Full credential oversight.</td><td><code>[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="bp">Executive</span></td><td>Strategic oversight</td><td>Edit on operational modules. Full financial visibility. Modular User Manual.</td><td>Can see and manage Team and User only. Peers and Admins hidden. Blocked from SRC.</td><td><code>ExecutiveOnly / UsersController</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="bb">Team</span></td><td>Day-to-day operations</td><td>Configurable per-module Read or Edit. Modular User Manual.</td><td>Self-only profile (/Users/Profile). Cannot view other users.</td><td><code>RequireModulePermission</code></td></tr>
                                <tr><td><span class="ba">User</span></td><td>Restricted field access</td><td>Read access to assigned modules. Modular User Manual.</td><td>Self-only profile (/Users/Profile). Cannot view other users.</td><td><code>PermissionAuthorization.cs</code></td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>16.2 Single Active Session Token &amp; Authentication Middleware</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/SessionValidationMiddleware.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Controllers/AccountController.cs</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>Cookie Authentication:</strong> HttpOnly signed cookies using <code>CookieAuthenticationDefaults</code>, bound to server Data Protection key ring.</li>
                        <li><strong>Password Hashing:</strong> BCrypt adaptive hashing via <code>PasswordService</code> with configurable iteration count. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/PasswordService.cs</span>]</span></li>
                        <li><strong>Single Active Session:</strong> Every login generates a new <code>ActiveSessionToken</code> in DB. The <code>SessionValidationMiddleware</code> invalidates earlier browser sessions if a newer token exists. <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/SessionValidationMiddleware.cs</span>]</span></li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>16.3 Downward-Only Peer Isolation &amp; Live Password Oversight</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Controllers/UsersController.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Users/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Users/Profile.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li><strong>Peer-Isolation Query Filter:</strong> In <code>UsersController.Index</code>, accounts at the caller's tier or higher are excluded from the dataset. Executives only view Team and User records. Team and User roles are redirected directly to <code>/Users/Profile</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Live Plaintext Password Inspection:</strong> Managers (Admin &amp; Executive) can toggle-view and copy subordinate plaintext passwords directly from the user table. When employees change their password on <code>/Users/Profile</code>, updates sync immediately for their managers.</li>
                        <li><strong>Strict Admin Gate for SRC:</strong> The System Requirements Contract (SRC) endpoints (<code>/Documents/Src</code>, <code>DownloadSrcPdf</code>, <code>ViewSrcPdf</code>) are decorated with <code>[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]</code>. Executives and operational users receive 403 Forbidden or login redirects.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
