                <section id="sec-20" class="src-section">
                    <div class="sec-label">Section 20.0</div>
                    <h2 class="sec-h2">
                        <span>20. Batch Color Mapping Algorithm</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/BatchColorHelper.cs</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Devices/Index.cshtml</span> &bull; <span class="b-file">Views/Inventory/Index.cshtml</span>]</span>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="sec-p">Each unique InvoiceId/batch name is assigned a persistent, algorithmically generated color badge for visual identification across large tabular grids:</p>
                    <h3 class="sec-h3">
                        <span>20.1 Golden Angle Hue Generation &amp; Alias Resolution</span>
                        <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">Services/BatchColorHelper.cs</span>: <span class="b-action">GetBatchColor(), RtoBatchToInvoiceMap</span>]</span>
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="sec-ul">
                        <li>All unique InvoiceId values collected from full device set (ignoring branch filter for RTO batch aliases). <span class="file-bracket">[<span class="b-file">BatchColorHelper.cs</span>]</span></li>
                        <li>Sorted deterministically: numeric IDs sorted numerically, then alphabetically.</li>
                        <li>Each batch index <em>i</em> &rarr; HSL color: <strong>Hue = (i &times; 137.508&deg;) mod 360</strong>, Saturation &asymp; 65&ndash;75%, Lightness &asymp; 45&ndash;55%.</li>
                        <li>Golden angle (&asymp;137.508&deg;) ensures maximum perceptual separation even across 50+ batches.</li>
                        <li><code>BatchColorHelper.RtoBatchToInvoiceMap</code> provides alias resolution so RTO batch names map to canonical invoice numbers.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
